    "Question #: 7": {
      "Title": "Exam 300-365 topic 1 question 37 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which two methods to discover a controller does a MAP attempt when it boots up? (Choose two.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. If Ethernet and wireless are available, it attempts to discover only via Ethernet."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. If Ethernet is disconnected, it attempts to connect wirelessly using AWPP."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. If only wireless is available and it is configured as a MAP, it does not attempt to connect to a WLC."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. If Ethernet and wireless are available, it uses Ethernet first. If it cannot connect via Ethernet, then it chooses wireless."
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. If Ethernet is disconnected, it attempts to connect wirelessly using the configured DHCP option."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: AB \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "References: http://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/wireless/controller/7-3/configuration/guide/b_cg73/b_wlc-cg_chapter_01001.html"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
